    "narrative": "The mandate for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is maximizing high-floor offensive production against a slate featuring several soft matchups. **Corbin Carroll** (77.67) stands as our premier play, benefiting from a prime matchup against Lodolo; with an elite score bolstered by a favorable SP xERA of 4.68 and a high-leverage spot in the two-hole, **Corbin Carroll** is our primary engine for SB and R production. **Gabriel Moreno** (65.17) and **Isaac Paredes** (62.39) also offer significant upside today; **Gabriel Moreno** benefits from a strong platoon advantage and a favorable order placement, while **Isaac Paredes** continues to capitalize on positive SP xERA environments, providing essential stability at the 3B slot.\n\nThe most difficult personnel decision centered on **Cole Young** (44.33). Despite his elite ability to rack up steals\u2014a category we weigh heavily\u2014he was the odd man out in a crowded outfield and utility rotation. His score sat just below the threshold required to displace **Mickey Moniak**, who, despite a harsh platoon disadvantage, benefits from a massive park factor boost that the model projects will outweigh the stolen base potential of **Cole Young** in today\u2019s specific environment. Elsewhere, we remain cautious regarding **Brice Turang** (45.73); while his order placement is excellent, facing an elite arm like Sale (2.83 xERA) represents a significant drag on his overall efficiency, making him a marginal start that we are monitoring closely.\n\nWe are forced to navigate around significant roster attrition, as **Trevor Story** and **James Wood** remain sidelined on the IL, limiting our late-game tactical flexibility. While we have deep reserves like **Austin Riley**, his matchup against a dominant Misiorowski (2.09 xERA) makes him an easy exclusion today. We will be looking for late-inning contributions from the rest of the bench\u2014including **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Henry Bolte**\u2014should any of our starters falter against their respective assignments. Watch the late-afternoon weather reports closely, as any wind shifts in the parks hosting **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Josh Naylor** could necessitate a recalibration of our expected power output.",
